  "reference_notes": "Compared the erect tuft and streamside arching-frond photographs, then all three current sizes and all 36 variants. The final model carries distinct curved rachises, opposite pinnae, and secondary pinnules aligned to the rachis tangent; upright and spreading fronds now coexist instead of horizontal shelves. The 36 variants retain connected bases and varied open silhouettes across 0.42\u20131.05 m heights. At the small end, pinnae merge into voxel ladders; microscopic sori and individual leaflet serrations are intentionally unresolved at 25 mm. Accepted as a stylized spring male fern source, separate from user variant endorsement.",
